# MAD Gambit — Environment Variables
# Copy to .env.local for development. Never commit .env with real values.
#
# On Vercel these live in Project → Settings → Environment Variables (per
# Production / Preview / Development). Anything a browser must read is prefixed
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ (inlined at build time — never put secrets behind that prefix).
#
# Every variable below is read by code in this app (file named per entry).
# Vars are grouped by WHO sets them. Full provisioning walkthrough:
# docs/MAD_GAMBIT_MASTER.md (Part II)

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# INJECTED BY VERCEL INTEGRATIONS — do not set these by hand on Vercel.
# For local dev, pull real values with `vercel env pull .env.local` or set
# them manually here.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Postgres (Neon via the Vercel Marketplace integration). Read by
# lib/database-url.ts, which also accepts POSTGRES_URL, POSTGRES_PRISMA_URL,
# and legacy project-prefixed integration names as fallbacks.
# Optional at runtime: API routes degrade to demo/fallback data when unset.
# Required only when running the controlled `npm run migrate:deploy` or `npm run schema:verify` commands.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/madgambit

# Redis (Upstash via the Vercel Marketplace integration). Server-only cache,
# rate-limit, or queue code can use these injected values. This application has
# no Redis client yet, so do not add a browser-visible NEXT_PUBLIC_ variant.
REDIS_URL=
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=

# Vercel Blob store credentials (auto-injected when a Blob store is connected).
# lib/vercel-blob-store.ts uses these only on the server for private encrypted
# portrait payloads. Never expose this token to browser code.
BLOB_STORE_ID=
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECRETS YOU SET — required for full functionality; each fails closed.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Gemini key for the MADHAT'r concierge + satire engine + embeddings
# (app/api/concierge/chat, app/api/satire-engine, lib/vector-store.ts).
# NOTE: the code reads GOOGLE_API_KEY, not GEMINI_API_KEY.
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GOOGLE_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key-here

# NVIDIA NIM for the MADHAT'r concierge (optional — tried BEFORE Gemini; both unset = knowledge file only).
# Both NIM_API_KEY and NIM_MODEL must be set to switch it on. Server-side only; never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
NIM_API_KEY=
# Primary model. Production runs nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni-30b-a3b-reasoning (a 30B mixture-of-experts, ~3B active,
# thinking on: 2 to 8 s a reply). nvidia/nemotron-3.5-bolt-e4b answers in ~1 s with no thinking. A reasoning model's
# thinking counts against max_tokens, so give it room with NIM_THINKING_HEADROOM or it can return an empty reply.
NIM_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni-30b-a3b-reasoning
# NIM_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1   # default; set to your own NIM host's /v1 URL if you self-host
# NIM_FALLBACK_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3.5-bolt-e4b   # tried when the primary fails, times out or answers nothing; the primary is then skipped for 2 min
# NIM_TIMEOUT_MS=12000          # how long the primary may take (2000-60000, default 8000); the fallback always gets 8000
# NIM_THINKING_HEADROOM=700     # extra tokens (0-4000) added to the primary's max_tokens when it thinks
# NIM_THINKING=off              # optional: turn thinking off for the primary everywhere. Calls that must return strict JSON
#                               # (the satire roast) and one-liners (the quip, the ticker caption) already turn it off per call.

# ── Local model roast tier (optional) ────────────────────────────────
# A model running on YOUR machine writes the satirical one-liners, tried
# BEFORE Gemini in app/api/satire-engine and used exclusively by the public
# POST /api/v1/satire/roast (which never reaches a metered API, by design).
#
# Ollama listens on the machine that started it, so a Vercel serverless
# function CANNOT reach your desktop: leave these unset in a normal Vercel
# deployment and the route degrades to the deterministic writer, as it always
# has. Set them for local development, or for a self-hosted deployment where
# the model sits beside the app.
#
#   ollama serve
#   ollama pull <model>          # then put that exact tag in OLLAMA_MODEL
#
# BOTH must be set or the tier stays off. Non-http(s) schemes are refused.
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434
OLLAMA_MODEL=

# HMAC key for signed session cookies (lib/session.ts). Without it, SIWE
# sign-in verifies but issues NO cookie → all wallet-authed routes 401.
# Generate: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
SESSION_SECRET=your-64-hex-char-session-secret-here

# Bearer secret for scheduled jobs (lib/bearer-secret.ts). Vercel Cron sends
# `Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET` automatically to the crons declared in
# vercel.json (rollup / perps roll / registrar lapse). Routes 503 when unset.
CRON_SECRET=your-cron-shared-secret-here

# x-pause-guardian header secret for the emergency-halt route
# (app/api/v1/registrar/pause). Guardian actions are refused when unset.
PAUSE_GUARDIAN_TOKEN=your-guardian-token-here

# HMAC pepper for the real-person ↔ subjectRef identity index
# (lib/subject-identity-map.ts). Identity-index writes THROW when unset.
# REGISTRAR_PEPPER is honored as a legacy alias.
SUBJECT_MAP_PEPPER=your-identity-pepper-here

# Gasless relayer's own wallet (app/api/v1/relay/execute) — submits
# ERC-2771 meta-transactions on behalf of users and pays their gas. This key
# holds real ETH for gas; treat it like a hot wallet, not an API key. Route
# 503s (relaying disabled, direct on-chain calls still work) when unset.
# Generate a dedicated wallet for this — never reuse the contract deployer key.
RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY=your-relayer-wallet-private-key-here

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# OPTIONAL
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Extra HTTP Basic guest login for the access gate (proxy.ts), added on top
# of the pairs in GUEST_LOGINS. Set both or neither. There are no built-in
# pairs: with neither variable set, the gate refuses everyone.
GUEST_USER=
GUEST_PASS=

# Override the built-in GDELT scandal/celebrity query (lib/gdelt-ingest.ts).
GDELT_QUERY=

# Legacy migration-runner escape hatch. Do not set this in Vercel; normal builds
# never run migrations.
SKIP_MIGRATIONS=

# RPC endpoint the relayer submits transactions through. Optional — falls
# back to viem's default public Arbitrum One RPC, which is fine for low
# volume but worth overriding with a dedicated provider (Alchemy/Infura) once
# relay traffic is real; public RPCs rate-limit.
RELAYER_RPC_URL=

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PUBLIC CONTRACT ADDRESSES (front/back SYNC — read by lib/contracts.ts)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ so the client and API routes resolve the SAME addresses.
# All optional: lib/contracts.ts has hardcoded fallbacks on chain 42161
# (Arbitrum One); unset non-MADx addresses render as "not deployed".
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# $MADx canonical address, confirmed on Arbitrum One (42161) — see
# script/Deploy.s.sol's DEFAULT_MADX and docs/MAD_GAMBIT_MASTER.md.
# Leaving this unset uses that same fallback; only set it to override.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MADX_ADDRESS=
NEXT_PUBLIC_STAKING_ADDRESS=
NEXT_PUBLIC_MARKET_FACTORY_ADDRESS=
NEXT_PUBLIC_TREASURY_ADDRESS=
# ERC2771Forwarder deployed by script/Deploy.s.sol — both MADStaking and
# MADMarketFactory trust this address. Required for gasless relaying to work;
# direct (non-relayed) on-chain calls don't need it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FORWARDER_ADDRESS=

# ── Platform-owned (do NOT set on Vercel) ─────────────────────────────
# NODE_ENV, PORT, NEXT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED are managed by the platform
# (Vercel build/runtime; Dockerfile sets them for the Cloud Run image).
